{"type":"message","id":"0e323991","parentId":"0424a975","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:56:17.834Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the config, I can see:\n\n1. **Feishu channel**: `dmPolicy: 'allowlist'`, with `allowFrom: ['ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683']` - this means only VAN can message through Feishu.\n\n2. **Kimi channel**: There's no `dmPolicy` or `allowFrom` configured in the kimi-claw config. The Kimi bridge connects via WebSocket to `wss://www.kimi.com/api-claw/bots/agent-ws` with a bot-token. This means it's a 1-on-1 chat with the bot, not a group chat. Anyone who has access to the Kimi bot can message.\n   \n   The question is whether other people in a Kimi group chat can see and respond to messages. Since Kimi uses a bot-token with WebSocket, it's likely configured as a 1-on-1 chat rather than a group chat, but I need to check the kimi-claw plugin documentation to confirm whether it supports group chats or if it's limited to direct messages with the bot.\n\nI should also look at whether there's an allowlist or access control mechanism for the Kimi channel, similar to what Feishu has with its `allowFrom` list, to determine if there's any restriction on who can interact with the bot.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"从配置看：\n\n**飞书** ✅ 安全 — `dmPolicy: allowlist`，只有你的飞书 ID (`ou_1a64...`) 可以私聊\n\n**Kimi** — 配置里**没有设置 allowlist**：\n```\nkimi-claw:\n  enabled: true\n  config:\n    bridge:\n      url: wss://www.kimi.com/api-claw/bots/agent-ws\n      token: (已配置)\n```\n\n这意味着：\n- 如果是 Kimi **1对1聊天** — 只有你能跟 bot 对话，没问题\n- 如果是 Kimi **群聊** — 群内所有人都能看到 bot 的消息并 @它\n\n**需要你确认：** 你在 Kimi 那边是 1对1 还是群聊？如果是群聊，建议加上限制。要我查一下 kimi-claw 是否支持 `allowFrom` 配置？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":20638,"output":803,"cacheRead":76224,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":97665,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stop